Subject: [PATCH] extras: Treat an empty primary ICC profile as invalid

When the codestream carries an ICC profile with an unknown color space, the
JXL decoder sets primary_color_representation to kIccIsPrimary but leaves
ppf.icc empty. ConvertPackedPixelFileToCodecInOut() then calls
ColorEncoding::SetICC() with an empty profile, which aborts on
JXL_ENSURE(!icc.empty()). Fall back to sRGB as for any other profile that
SetICC() rejects.

Found with the set_from_bytes fuzzer (abort in
ConvertPackedPixelFileToCodecInOut < SetFromBytes).
Reproducer: repro/fix-convert-empty-primary-icc.jxl.
Test: CodecTest.ConvertEmptyPrimaryICC.
---
